{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1904","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1904/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1904/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1904/events","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/1904","id":3057215625,"node_id":"I_kwDOLW-eZs62OWiJ","number":1904,"title":"[field] Option or way to run the validation function after checkValidity","user":{"login":"benjavicente","id":62021328,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyMDIxMzI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62021328?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benjavicente","html_url":"https://github.com/benjavicente","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benjavicente/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benjavicente/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benjavicente/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benjavicente/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benjavicente/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benjavicente/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benjavicente/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benjavicente/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benjavicente/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7205061925,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLW-eZs8AAAABrXSFJQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/labels/component:%20field","name":"component: field","color":"ffffff","default":false,"description":"Changes related to the field component.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":8032553743,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLW-eZs8AAAAB3scLDw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/labels/has%20workaround","name":"has workaround","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"There’s a bug, but users have a complete workaround, so no urgent fix or release is needed.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-05-12T14:39:52Z","updated_at":"2025-05-20T06:14:35Z","closed_at":"2025-05-20T06:14:35Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Feature request\n\n## Summary\n\nIn a Field, I want to run a validation only after the native input validation has run, such that a `customError`is only shown if there aren't any non-custom errors. \n\nHere is a codepen: https://codesandbox.io/p/sandbox/clever-chihiro-ssw6fd?file=%2Fsrc%2FApp.tsx\n\nSee that `Field.Error` with `customError` is rendered when the pattern is also invalid.\n\nOn those cases, the preferred way would be to use a validation library like zod, or there is an intended way to run a validation function **after** the validity of the input was checked?\n\nA way to hack around this limitation would be to get a ref of the input element and run `checkValidity` inside the validation function. Uncomment the first line of the validation function to see that.\n\n\n## Examples in other libraries\n\nCouldn't find a similar example.\n\n## Motivation\n\nMy use case is to run a [chek digit](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Check_digit) function **after** the field is completed (passing required validation) and if it matches a regular expression (patter validation). I want to avoid repeating code, ej validating the pattern on the validation function and on the element itself.\n","closed_by":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1904/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1904/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}